    "Fees are public fee schedules. The kraken and binance symbol overrides are MEASURED: mean half-spread,",
    "median depth and a fitted impact coefficient from the recorder's top-20 books, 2026-09-30 to 2026-10-07",
    "(research/lab, experiment costs; re-run it and paste its calibrated block to refresh). Every other venue",
    "default and override is still a guess from typical quoted spreads, waiting for recorded data.",
    "Units: every *Bps field is basis points (1 bp = 0.01 %). Fees are the lowest-volume retail tier.",
    "halfSpreadBps is per side: what a taker pays against the mid. impactCoeff is the extra cost in bps when",
    "an order's notional equals the book depth on the side it takes, scaled by sqrt(notional / depth)",
    "(the square-root law). Depth means the notional on the 20 best levels of that side, in quote currency",
    "(USD), which is what a depth20 feed reports; defaultDepth is its median, used when no live book is",
    "available. minNotional is the smallest order the venue accepts, in USD, approximately.",
    "symbols overrides any field for one instrument, keyed by base asset (BTC) or ticker (AAPL).",
    "Fee sources (lowest tier, checked 2026): Kraken Pro spot 0.25 % maker / 0.40 % taker; Binance spot",
    "0.10 / 0.10; Bybit spot 0.10 / 0.10; OKX spot 0.08 maker / 0.10 taker; Coinbase Advanced 0.40 / 0.60;",
    "Alpaca US equities commission-free (SEC and FINRA TAF regulatory fees on sells are well under 1 bp and",
    "are not modelled); Polymarket charges no trading fee on most markets, so the spread is the cost."
